<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Architecture v2 (updated) - 4x4 Weight-Stationary Systolic Accelerator</title>
<style>
:root{
  --bg:#ffffff; --fg:#15181d; --muted:#5d6673; --line:#e3e7ed; --line2:#cdd4de;
  --panel:#f7f9fb; --panel2:#eef2f7; --code:#f4f6f9;
  --accent:#0b5fd0; --accent-w:#e7f0fd;
  --w:#1747c9;  --wbg:#e8eeff;
  --a:#b4470b;  --abg:#fdefe4;
  --p:#0d7a49;  --pbg:#e4f6ec;
  --idle:#8a94a3; --warn:#9a6700; --bad:#b42318;
  --mono:ui-monospace,"Cascadia Mono","SFMono-Regular",Consolas,"Liberation Mono",monospace;
  --sans:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",Roboto,"Helvetica Neue",Arial,sans-serif;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){
  :root{
    --bg:#0f1216; --fg:#e6eaf0; --muted:#9aa5b4; --line:#242a33; --line2:#333b47;
    --panel:#161b21; --panel2:#1c222a; --code:#141920;
    --accent:#5aa2ff; --accent-w:#132234;
    --w:#7fa8ff; --wbg:#16223c;
    --a:#f0a06a; --abg:#33210f;
    --p:#5ed49a; --pbg:#0f2a1e;
    --idle:#6b7482; --warn:#e0b341; --bad:#f28b82;
  }
}
*{box-sizing:border-box}
html{scroll-behavior:smooth}
body{
  margin:0; background:var(--bg); color:var(--fg);
  font-family:var(--sans); font-size:16px; line-height:1.65;
  -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
}
.wrap{max-width:1180px; margin:0 auto; padding:0 28px 120px}
header.masthead{
  border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); padding:56px 0 34px; margin-bottom:34px;
}
.eyebrow{font-size:12px; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--accent); font-weight:700; margin:0 0 12px}
h1{font-size:clamp(28px,4.4vw,44px); line-height:1.14; margin:0 0 14px; letter-spacing:-.022em; font-weight:750}
.sub{font-size:18px; color:var(--muted); margin:0 0 22px; max-width:74ch}
.meta{display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px}
.chip{
  font-size:12.5px; font-family:var(--mono); background:var(--panel);
  border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:999px; padding:4px 12px; color:var(--muted);
}
.chip.ok{color:var(--p); border-color:var(--p); background:var(--pbg)}
h2{font-size:26px; margin:56px 0 6px; letter-spacing:-.015em; font-weight:720; scroll-margin-top:20px}
h2 .num{color:var(--accent); font-family:var(--mono); font-size:19px; margin-right:10px; font-weight:600}
h3{font-size:19.5px; margin:34px 0 6px; letter-spacing:-.01em; font-weight:680}
h4{font-size:16px; margin:24px 0 4px; font-weight:680; color:var(--fg)}
h2+p,h3+p,h4+p{margin-top:8px}
p{margin:0 0 15px; max-width:82ch}
ul,ol{max-width:82ch; padding-left:24px; margin:0 0 15px}
li{margin:5px 0}
a{color:var(--accent); text-decoration:none; border-bottom:1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, transparent)}
a:hover{border-bottom-color:var(--accent)}
code{font-family:var(--mono); font-size:.88em; background:var(--code); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:4px; padding:1px 5px}
pre{
  font-family:var(--mono); font-size:13px; line-height:1.62; background:var(--code);
  border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:8px; padding:16px 18px; overflow-x:auto; margin:0 0 18px;
}
pre code{background:none; border:0; padding:0; font-size:inherit}
.cmt{color:var(--muted)}
.kw{color:var(--accent); font-weight:600}
.num2{color:var(--a)}
table{border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; margin:0 0 20px; font-size:14.5px; display:block; overflow-x:auto}
th,td{border:1px solid var(--line); padding:8px 12px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top}
th{background:var(--panel); font-weight:650; font-size:13px; letter-spacing:.02em}
tbody tr:nth-child(even){background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel) 55%, transparent)}
td code{font-size:.9em}
.note,.warnbox,.keybox{
  border-left:3px solid var(--accent); background:var(--accent-w);
  padding:14px 18px; border-radius:0 8px 8px 0; margin:0 0 20px; font-size:15px;
}
.note p:last-child,.warnbox p:last-child,.keybox p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
.warnbox{border-left-color:var(--warn); background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 10%, transparent)}
.keybox{border-left-color:var(--p); background:var(--pbg)}
.lbl{font-size:11.5px; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.1em; font-weight:750; display:block; margin-bottom:4px}
.note .lbl{color:var(--accent)} .warnbox .lbl{color:var(--warn)} .keybox .lbl{color:var(--p)}
.toc{background:var(--panel); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:10px; padding:20px 24px; margin:0 0 20px}
.toc ol{columns:2; column-gap:44px; margin:0; padding-left:20px; font-size:14.5px}
.toc li{margin:3px 0; break-inside:avoid}
figure{margin:0 0 24px}
figcaption{font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted); margin-top:10px; max-width:82ch}
figcaption b{color:var(--fg)}
.diagram{background:var(--panel); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:10px; padding:20px; overflow-x:auto}
.diagram svg{display:block; margin:0 auto; max-width:100%; height:auto}

/* ---------- animation widget ---------- */
.stage{
  border:1px solid var(--line2); border-radius:12px; background:var(--panel);
  margin:0 0 14px; overflow:hidden;
}
.stage-bar{
  display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:center; gap:10px;
  padding:10px 14px; background:var(--panel2); border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);
}
.btn{
  font:inherit; font-size:13px; font-weight:600; padding:5px 13px; border-radius:7px;
  border:1px solid var(--line2); background:var(--bg); color:var(--fg); cursor:pointer;
}
.btn:hover{border-color:var(--accent); color:var(--accent)}
.btn.primary{background:var(--accent); color:#fff; border-color:var(--accent)}
.btn.primary:hover{filter:brightness(1.1); color:#fff}
.cyc{font-family:var(--mono); font-size:14px; font-weight:700; padding:4px 10px; background:var(--bg); border:1px solid var(--line2); border-radius:7px}
.phase{
  font-family:var(--mono); font-size:12px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.08em;
  padding:4px 11px; border-radius:999px; color:#fff; background:var(--idle);
}
.phase[data-p="WLOAD"]{background:var(--w)}
.phase[data-p="FLUSH"]{background:var(--idle)}
.phase[data-p="COMPUTE"]{background:var(--p)}
.phase[data-p="DRAIN"]{background:var(--a)}
.phase[data-p="DONE"]{background:var(--accent)}
.spacer{flex:1}
.stage-body{padding:18px 14px}
.hint{font-size:12.5px; color:var(--muted); font-family:var(--mono)}
input[type=range]{accent-color:var(--accent)}

/* timeline */
.tl{display:flex; height:22px; border-radius:6px; overflow:hidden; border:1px solid var(--line2); margin:0 14px 0 0; min-width:260px; flex:1}
.tl div{display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size:10px; font-family:var(--mono); font-weight:700; color:#fff; opacity:.42; transition:opacity .15s}
.tl div.on{opacity:1}
.tl .t-w{background:var(--w)} .tl .t-f{background:var(--idle)} .tl .t-c{background:var(--p)} .tl .t-d{background:var(--a)} .tl .t-o{background:var(--accent)}

/* array grid */
.arrwrap{display:grid; grid-template-columns:auto auto 1fr; gap:0 10px; align-items:start; overflow-x:auto}
.cellgrid{display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(84px,1fr)); gap:6px}
.pe{
  position:relative; background:var(--bg); border:1px solid var(--line2); border-radius:8px;
  padding:20px 6px 6px; min-height:64px; text-align:center; transition:background .12s,border-color .12s;
}
.pe.acc{border-color:var(--p); background:var(--pbg); box-shadow:0 0 0 2px color-mix(in srgb,var(--p) 22%,transparent)}
.pe.shift{border-color:var(--w); background:var(--wbg)}
.pe .wq{position:absolute; top:3px; left:6px; font:600 10.5px var(--mono); color:var(--w)}
.pe .aq{position:absolute; top:3px; right:6px; font:600 10.5px var(--mono); color:var(--a)}
.pe .pq{font:700 15px var(--mono); color:var(--p); line-height:1.2}
.pe .pq.zero{color:var(--muted); font-weight:500}
.pe .tag{position:absolute; bottom:2px; right:5px; font:500 9px var(--mono); color:var(--muted)}
.edge{display:grid; gap:6px; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(84px,1fr))}
.eb{
  background:var(--bg); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:6px; padding:4px 2px;
  text-align:center; font:600 12.5px var(--mono); min-height:26px;
}
.eb.w{color:var(--w); background:var(--wbg); border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--w) 30%,transparent)}
.eb.p{color:var(--p)}
.eb.hot{background:var(--pbg); border-color:var(--p); font-weight:700}
.eb.dim{color:var(--muted); background:transparent}
.rowlab{display:grid; gap:6px; font:600 11px var(--mono); color:var(--muted); text-align:right; padding-right:2px}
.rowlab div{height:64px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:flex-end}
.wl{display:grid; gap:6px}
.wl .cellv{
  height:64px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; min-width:52px;
  background:var(--bg); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:6px;
  font:700 13px var(--mono); color:var(--a);
}
.wl .cellv.off{color:var(--muted); font-weight:400; background:transparent}
.wl .cellv.live{background:var(--abg); border-color:var(--a)}
.colhdr{display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(84px,1fr)); gap:6px; font:600 11px var(--mono); color:var(--muted); text-align:center; margin-bottom:3px}
.sect-lab{font:600 11px var(--mono); color:var(--muted); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.08em; margin:14px 0 4px}
.legend{display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:14px; font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); margin-top:14px}
.legend span{display:flex; align-items:center; gap:6px}
.sw{width:11px; height:11px; border-radius:3px; display:inline-block}

/* pipe animation */
.pipeline{display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; flex-wrap:wrap; justify-content:center; padding:10px 0}
.slot{
  width:56px; height:46px; border:1px solid var(--line2); border-radius:8px; background:var(--bg);
  display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font:700 15px var(--mono); position:relative;
}
.slot.stage{border-color:var(--accent)}
.slot .cap{position:absolute; top:-17px; left:0; right:0; text-align:center; font:600 9.5px var(--mono); color:var(--muted)}
.slot.din{border-style:dashed; color:var(--a)}
.slot.dout{border-color:var(--p); color:var(--p); background:var(--pbg)}
.arrow{color:var(--muted); font-size:17px}

/* trace tables */
.trace{max-height:430px; overflow:auto; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:9px; margin:0 0 22px}
.trace table{margin:0; border:0; font-size:12.5px; font-family:var(--mono); display:table}
.trace th{position:sticky; top:0; z-index:2; background:var(--panel2); font-family:var(--sans); border-top:0}
.trace td,.trace th{padding:4px 9px; white-space:nowrap; border-color:var(--line)}
.trace .hi{background:var(--pbg); font-weight:700; color:var(--p)}
.trace .wl2{background:var(--wbg); color:var(--w)}
.trace .mut{color:var(--muted)}
.tcap{font-size:13px; color:var(--muted); margin:0 0 6px}

.pill{display:inline-block; font:600 11px var(--mono); padding:2px 8px; border-radius:999px; border:1px solid var(--line2); color:var(--muted); background:var(--panel)}
.pill.ok{color:var(--p); border-color:var(--p); background:var(--pbg)}
.pill.bad{color:var(--bad); border-color:var(--bad)}
.grid2{display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr)); gap:18px; margin:0 0 20px}
.card{border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:10px; padding:16px 18px; background:var(--panel)}
.card h4{margin-top:0}
.card p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
hr{border:0; border-top:1px solid var(--line); margin:44px 0}
.foot{border-top:1px solid var(--line); margin-top:60px; padding-top:22px; font-size:13.5px; color:var(--muted)}
.printonly{display:none}

@media (max-width:760px){
  .wrap{padding:0 16px 80px}
  .toc ol{columns:1}
  .cellgrid,.edge,.colhdr{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(66px,1fr))}
}
@media print{
  :root{
    --bg:#fff; --fg:#000; --muted:#444; --line:#bbb; --line2:#999;
    --panel:#f6f6f6; --panel2:#eee; --code:#f6f6f6; --accent:#0b5fd0;
    --wbg:#e8eeff; --abg:#fdefe4; --pbg:#e4f6ec;
  }
  body{font-size:10pt; line-height:1.48}
  .wrap{max-width:none; padding:0}
  .stage-bar .btn,.stage-bar input,.stage-bar .spacer,.stage-bar label{display:none !important}
  /* nothing may be clipped on paper: every scroll container becomes a flow container */
  table{display:table; overflow:visible; font-size:8.6pt; table-layout:fixed; word-break:break-word}
  th,td{padding:4px 7px}
  pre{overflow:visible; white-space:pre-wrap; word-break:break-word; font-size:8.4pt; line-height:1.5}
  .diagram,.arrwrap,.trace,.pipeline{overflow:visible}
  .trace{max-height:none; page-break-inside:auto}
  .trace table{font-size:7.6pt; table-layout:auto}
  .trace td,.trace th{white-space:normal; padding:2.5px 5px}
  .trace th{position:static}
  .cellgrid,.edge,.colhdr,.dsk{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr)}
  .pe{height:56px} .rowlab div,.wl .cellv{height:56px}
  .pe .pq{font-size:12px}
  .toc ol{columns:2}
  h2{page-break-after:avoid; margin-top:24pt} h3,h4{page-break-after:avoid}
  figure,.stage,.note,.warnbox,.keybox,.card,.grid2{page-break-inside:avoid}
  pre,table{page-break-inside:auto}
  .printonly{display:block}
  a{color:#000; border:0}
  header.masthead{padding-top:0}
  @page{margin:15mm 12mm}
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

<header class="masthead">
  <p class="eyebrow">Technical Reference Â· Design &amp; Verification</p>
  <h1>4Ã—4 Weight-Stationary Systolic Accelerator</h1>
  <p class="sub">Complete architecture, RTL structure and cycle-level data flow of a 13-module
  SystemVerilog matrix-multiply engine â€” with cycle-accurate animations of the delay pipes,
  the skew buffers and the systolic array itself.</p>
  <div class="meta">
    <span class="chip">13 RTL modules</span>
    <span class="chip">13 testbenches</span>
    <span class="chip ok">13/13 PASS Â· 3 902 checks Â· 0 mismatches</span>
    <span class="chip">int8 Ã— int8 â†’ int32</span>
    <span class="chip">QuestaSim 2021.1</span>
    <span class="chip">2026-07-30</span>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="printonly note">
  <span class="lbl">Reading this as a PDF</span>
  <p>Every animated figure in the HTML edition is followed here by its <b>complete cycle-by-cycle
  trace table</b>, generated by the same cycle-accurate model that drives the animation. Nothing is
  lost â€” the tables contain every value the animation would show, for every clock edge. Open
  <code>architecture_and_dataflow.html</code> to interact with them.</p>
</div>

<nav class="toc">
  <ol>
    <li><a href="#s1">What the design does</a></li>
    <li><a href="#s2">Repository and module map</a></li>
    <li><a href="#s3">Architecture: the three levels</a></li>
    <li><a href="#s4">Word formats and data layout</a></li>
    <li><a href="#s5">The processing element</a></li>
    <li><a href="#s6">delay_pipe â€” animated</a></li>
    <li><a href="#s7">The input skew buffer â€” animated</a></li>
    <li><a href="#s8">The systolic array</a></li>
    <li><a href="#s9">Matrix multiply, cycle by cycle â€” animated</a></li>
    <li><a href="#s10">The output de-skew buffer</a></li>
    <li><a href="#s11">The memories</a></li>
    <li><a href="#s12">Control plane: FSM and AGU</a></li>
    <li><a href="#s13">Timing derivations</a></li>
    <li><a href="#s14">End-to-end data flow</a></li>
    <li><a href="#s15">Verification summary</a></li>
    <li><a href="#s16">Known limitations</a></li>
  </ol>
</nav>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<h2 id="s1"><span class="num">1</span>What the design does</h2>

<p>The accelerator computes <b>C = A Ã— W</b>, where <code>W</code> is a stationary 4Ã—4 matrix of
8-bit signed integers and <code>A</code> is a stream of 4-element activation vectors. Each vector
produces one 4-element result vector of 32-bit signed integers, at a throughput of
<b>one vector per clock cycle</b> once the pipeline is full.</p>

<p>It is a <i>weight-stationary</i> systolic array. That phrase describes the dataflow completely:</p>

<div class="keybox">
  <span class="lbl">The dataflow in one sentence</span>
  <p><b>Weights enter from the north edge and stop; activations enter from the west and keep moving
  east; partial sums flow south and leave the bottom edge.</b></p>
</div>

<p>The weight matrix is loaded once into the 16 processing elements â€” one 8-bit weight each â€” and
then stays put. Activations stream through horizontally, and each processing element multiplies the
activation passing through it by its resident weight and adds the result to the partial sum
descending from above. By the time a partial sum leaves the bottom of a column it has accumulated
all four products of a dot product.</p>

<p>Nothing in the array is ever re-fetched from memory during compute. That is the entire point of
the architecture: a weight is read from SRAM once and then used for every activation vector in the
job. Memory bandwidth â€” not arithmetic â€” is what limits real machine-learning accelerators, so
minimising re-fetch is what makes the design fast.</p>

<h3>Key numbers</h3>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Value</th><th>Set by</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Array size</td><td>4 rows Ã— 4 columns = 16 processing elements</td><td><code>ROWS</code>, <code>COLS</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Operand format</td><td>int8 (signed, âˆ’128â€¦127)</td><td><code>DATA_W = 8</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Accumulator format</td><td>int32 (signed)</td><td><code>PSUM_W = 32</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Peak throughput</td><td>16 multiply-accumulates per clock</td><td>array size</td></tr>
<tr><td>Compute throughput</td><td>1 activation vector (4 MACs Ã— 4 columns) per clock</td><td>no back-pressure</td></tr>
<tr><td>Result latency</td><td>7 cycles from activation address to result on the bus</td><td><code>RESULT_LATENCY</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Store latency</td><td>8 cycles from activation address to write strobe</td><td><code>STORE_LATENCY</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Job length</td><td><code>num_vectors + 19</code> cycles</td><td>controller FSM</td></tr>
<tr><td>Activation memory</td><td>256 words Ã— 32 bits (256 vectors)</td><td><code>A_ADDR_W = 8</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Weight memory</td><td>4 words Ã— 32 bits (one word per weight row)</td><td><code>W_ADDR_W = 2</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Output memory</td><td>256 words Ã— 128 bits</td><td><code>O_ADDR_W = 8</code></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<h2 id="s2"><span class="num">2</span>Repository and module map</h2>

<pre><code>verification_individual/
â”œâ”€â”€ design_rtl/          13 synthesizable SystemVerilog files
â”œâ”€â”€ test_benches/        13 testbenches + run_all_testbenches.ps1
â”œâ”€â”€ indi_ver_rep/        verification report + raw QuestaSim transcripts
â”œâ”€â”€ DOCS/                description index + detailed docs (this file lives here)
â”œâ”€â”€ context_mkdwn/       derivations and design decisions
â”œâ”€â”€ docs_images/         architecture_overview.jpeg
â””â”€â”€ index.md             file locator</code></pre>

<h3>The 13 RTL modules</h3>

<table>
<thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>MAC.sv</code></td><td><code>processing_element</code></td><td>57</td><td>One weight-stationary multiply-accumulate cell</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>array.sv</code></td><td><code>systolic_array</code></td><td>63</td><td>4Ã—4 grid of PEs â€” pure interconnect, no arithmetic</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>delay_pipe.sv</code></td><td><code>delay_pipe</code></td><td>31</td><td>Parameterised <i>N</i>-deep shift register; <code>DELAY=0</code> is a wire</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>input_buf.sv</code></td><td><code>input_skew_buffer</code></td><td>35</td><td>Dense vector â†’ diagonal wavefront (row <i>r</i> delayed by <i>r</i>)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>output_skewbuf.sv</code></td><td><code>output_deskew_buffer</code></td><td>24</td><td>Removes the column staircase (column <i>c</i> delayed by <code>COLS-1-c</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>a_mem.sv</code></td><td><code>a_mem</code></td><td>19</td><td>Activation SRAM, 256 Ã— 32</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>weight_mem.sv</code></td><td><code>weight_mem</code></td><td>18</td><td>Weight SRAM, 4 Ã— 32</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>outmem.sv</code></td><td><code>output_mem</code></td><td>18</td><td>Result SRAM, 256 Ã— 128</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>controller.sv</code></td><td><code>controller</code></td><td>128</td><td>Phase FSM â€” owns durations, produces no addresses</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>agu.sv</code></td><td><code>agu</code></td><td>114</td><td>Address generator â€” owns addresses, holds no policy</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>wrapper_array_buf.sv</code></td><td><code>array_buf_top</code></td><td>100</td><td><b>Level 1</b> â€” skew + array + de-skew</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>wrapper_mem_arr_buf.sv</code></td><td><code>accelerator_top</code></td><td>175</td><td><b>Level 2</b> â€” level 1 + the three SRAMs</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>wrapper_full_system.sv</code></td><td><code>accelerator_system_top</code></td><td>205</td><td><b>Level 3</b> â€” level 2 + FSM + AGU + arbitration</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<div class="warnbox">
  <span class="lbl">Filename â‰  module name</span>
  <p>Eight files carry a module whose name differs from the filename. Search by module name and use
  this table: <code>processing_element</code>â†’<code>MAC.sv</code>,
  <code>systolic_array</code>â†’<code>array.sv</code>,
  <code>input_skew_buffer</code>â†’<code>input_buf.sv</code>,
  <code>output_deskew_buffer</code>â†’<code>output_skewbuf.sv</code>,
  <code>output_mem</code>â†’<code>outmem.sv</code>,
  <code>array_buf_top</code>â†’<code>wrapper_array_buf.sv</code>,
  <code>accelerator_top</code>â†’<code>wrapper_mem_arr_buf.sv</code>,
  <code>accelerator_system_top</code>â†’<code>wrapper_full_system.sv</code>.</p>
</div>

<h3>Instance hierarchy</h3>

<pre><code>accelerator_system_top                    wrapper_full_system.sv     LEVEL 3
â”œâ”€â”€ controller                            controller.sv
â”œâ”€â”€ agu                                   agu.sv
â””â”€â”€ accelerator_top                       wrapper_mem_arr_buf.sv     LEVEL 2
    â”œâ”€â”€ a_mem                             a_mem.sv
    â”œâ”€â”€ weight_mem                        weight_mem.sv
    â”œâ”€â”€ output_mem                        outmem.sv
    â””â”€â”€ array_buf_top                     wrapper_array_buf.sv       LEVEL 1
        â”œâ”€â”€ input_skew_buffer             input_buf.sv
        â”‚   â””â”€â”€ delay_pipe  Ã— 2Â·ROWS      delay_pipe.sv
        â”œâ”€â”€ systolic_array                array.sv
        â”‚   â””â”€â”€ processing_element Ã— 16   MAC.sv
        â””â”€â”€ output_deskew_buffer          output_skewbuf.sv
            â””â”€â”€ delay_pipe  Ã— COLS        delay_pipe.sv</code></pre>

<p>Twelve <code>delay_pipe</code> instances exist in total: eight inside the input skew buffer (four
for data, four for the matching valid bits) and four inside the de-skew buffer.</p>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<h2 id="s3"><span class="num">3</span>Architecture: the three levels</h2>

<p>Rather than one monolithic top module, the design closes at three abstraction levels, each in its
own file. <b>Each level instantiates the level below rather than re-wiring the fabric.</b></p>

