      <span><span class="sw" style="background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--line)"></span> idle (valid = 0)</span>
      <span>vector <b>A0</b> = [1, 2, 3, 4] &nbsp; <b>A1</b> = [5, âˆ’1, 0, 2] &nbsp; <b>A2</b> = [âˆ’2, 3, 1, 1]</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<figcaption><b>Figure 7.1 â€” dense in, diagonal out.</b> On the left, three complete vectors are
presented on three consecutive cycles. On the right, the array's west edge sees them staggered: row 0
immediately, row 1 one cycle later, row 3 three cycles later. Watch the <code>A0</code> elements form
a diagonal line down the right-hand column.</figcaption>
</figure>

